content:
{
  "asset": "P-104 standby unit, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump on the filtered-water line. The serial plate is painted over and unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable manufacturer criterion is Figure 3, expressed in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. Provided the reported 3.0 mm/s is an RMS bearing-housing reading, it is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary and below 4.5 mm/s, placing it in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s), 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C (4.5–7.1 mm/s, restricted—plan maintenance) and Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s, damage likely—stop the pump).",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature: the applicable HF-300 limits are for bearing temperature measured on the housing surface. At 69 C, the reading is within 'normal up to 70 C', 11 C below the 80 C alarm and 21 C below the 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage: the steady leak matches the manual's 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom. No numerical allowable leakage rate is supplied. The documented corrective action is mechanical seal replacement and an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No supplied rule requires an immediate stop or automatic priority-1 work order for the reported readings: immediate stop and reliability-engineer notification apply to vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, which this reading does not reach, and priority 1 within the shift applies to bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit, which 69 C does not exceed. P2 is a planning judgement for the steady leak, not a site-defined response classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "First inspection hypothesis: worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces, a documented probable cause of leakage at the shaft seal. Inspect the removed seal to confirm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Second inspection hypothesis: shaft misalignment. It is a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and is also listed for high vibration. The Zone B vibration reading does not confirm misalignment, but the manual specifically requires an alignment check for the leakage symptom.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Third inspection hypothesis: the seal has run dry, another documented cause of leakage. The pump has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; the report does not establish that dry running occurred.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Hold point before ordering or fitting a seal: establish the pump serial number from reliable asset or build records. For serial HF3-22000 and above, apply SB-2026-014 and do not fit HF3-450. Below HF3-22000, continue with HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Do not release the serial-dependent parts or gland torque until this is resolved.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Make the pump safe before seal work: electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; obtain a line-break permit and drain and vent before breaking the line. Isolate and drain the pump in accordance with seal-replacement procedure 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly. Its mass is 68 kg, so use the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment required for loads over 25 kg. The back pull-out design permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Inspect the removed seal for wear or cracking and record any evidence bearing on dry running or misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For serial HF3-22000 and above, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B; it is pre-set and needs no seal-setting sleeve measurement. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. For serial below HF3-22000, fit HF3-450 and follow the manual; do not apply the bulletin's sleeve rejection threshold outside its stated serial range.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the selected new seal and a new casing gasket, then reassemble. For Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, tighten M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. Seal gland torque is serial/seal dependent: M10 gland nuts for HF3-450 are 25 Nm under Table 5; HF3-450B gland nuts are 30 Nm under SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment for the seal-leakage symptom. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning the pump to operation or standby readiness, restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and ensure the pump is never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "SERIAL-DEPENDENT: HF3-450B or HF3-450",
      "description": "One mechanical seal only, selected after serial verification. Use HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above, where HF3-450 is prohibited; use HF3-450 only below HF3-22000. This entry does not authorise supplying both seals.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "Not specified in evidence",
      "description": "One new casing gasket for the HF-300 mechanical-seal replacement; obtain the correct gasket identification before assembly.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve, not confirmed as required: one only if the pump is within SB-2026-014's serial range and sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and use a line-break permit with draining and venting before line break.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold. Provide a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection and gland torque conflict: AQ-OM-300 Revision D Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set HF3-450B at 30 Nm for serial HF3-22000 and above. The bulletin explicitly retains HF3-450 and Table 5 below that serial. The serial-specific bulletin therefore governs only within its stated range; P-104's unreadable plate prevents a final selection. Decision: hold seal selection and gland torque until the serial is verified rather than defaulting to either document.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve instructions differ in scope: the manual requires inspection for scoring but gives no numerical rejection limit. For bulletin-covered pumps, HF3-450B needs no seal-setting sleeve measurement, while scoring greater than 0.1 mm requires HF3-455 replacement; this does not eliminate the scoring inspection. The 0.1 mm criterion is not extended here to pumps below the bulletin's serial cutoff.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What reliable record establishes P-104's serial number relative to HF3-22000? Until answered, the correct seal, gland torque and bulletin applicability remain unresolved (C13).",
    "Was the 3.0 mm/s vibration reading measured as RMS on a bearing housing, as required by Figure 3? If not, the Zone B classification must be confirmed using a compatible measurement (C07).",
    "Was the 69 C reading taken on the bearing-housing surface, to which the manual's bearing-temperature limits apply (C01, C02)?",
    "What is the correct part number or specification for the required new casing gasket? The manual requires the gasket but does not identify it (C10).",
    "What sleeve scoring depth is found on disassembly? If the serial is HF3-22000 or above, this determines whether HF3-455 is required. If the serial is below that cutoff, what sleeve reuse or rejection criterion applies, since the supplied manual gives no numerical limit (C10, C13)?",
    "What site response-time definitions distinguish P2 from P3, and what completion date is required? The supplied site procedure specifies a priority-1 trigger for bearing temperature above alarm but provides no P2/P3 definitions (C15)."
  ]
}
